08:10.000 --> 08:11.950
Eight.

08:12.000 --> 08:14.950
Wanted.

08:15.000 --> 08:16.950
Nine.

08:17.000 --> 08:19.000
Watched.

08:22.000 --> 08:23.950
Chapter Two.

08:24.000 --> 08:27.000
The Croft.

08:28.000 --> 08:33.950
The journey was uncomfortable in the pony and trap, as we trotted along the narrow roads.

08:34.000 --> 08:35.950
But it was fun too.

08:36.000 --> 08:42.950
I could see the bay, the seaweed and the rocks, and smell the salty sea.

08:43.000 --> 08:45.950
Sea gulls flew overhead.

08:46.000 --> 08:47.950
I looked at my uncle.

08:48.000 --> 08:51.950
He had my mother's smile, but they were very different.

08:52.000 --> 08:54.950
He saw me looking at him.

08:55.000 --> 08:58.950
So, this is your first visit to Skye Meghan.

08:59.000 --> 09:01.950
I'm so pleased you're here.

09:02.000 --> 09:02.950
He said,

09:03.000 --> 09:06.950
I want to bring Mum next time when she's better, I said.

09:07.000 --> 09:09.950
His eyes look sad.

09:10.000 --> 09:12.950
I want her to come here too.

09:13.000 --> 09:17.950
And then he took a deep breath, and there was silence.

09:18.000 --> 09:25.950
We trotted on through a forest, and then we stopped at a place where the view of the mountains was spectacular.

09:26.000 --> 09:27.950
The Kulin Range?

09:28.000 --> 09:29.950
Said Uncle Fraser.

09:30.000 --> 09:32.950
This is the best place to see the mountains.

09:33.000 --> 09:35.950
I got out of the trap and looked around.

09:36.000 --> 09:38.950
It was a magical place.

09:39.000 --> 09:42.950
There was a ruined castle and below a sandy beach.

09:43.000 --> 09:49.950
The waves crashed, and I thought I saw a silvery white horse playing in the water.

09:50.000 --> 09:54.950
It ran and jumped, and I am sure that I heard it call me.

09:55.000 --> 09:56.950
Uncle Fraser?

09:57.000 --> 09:58.950
I shouted.

09:59.000 --> 10:00.950
There's a white horse.

10:01.000 --> 10:02.950
He didn't hear me.

10:03.000 --> 10:07.950
And when I turned, the silvery white horse was not there.

10:08.000 --> 10:09.950
We got into the trap.

10:10.000 --> 10:13.950
I saw a silvery white horse down by the sea.

10:14.000 --> 10:14.950
I said,

10:15.000 --> 10:19.950
Uncle Fraser stopped and looked at me with surprise.

10:20.000 --> 10:20.950
Did you?

10:21.000 --> 10:22.950
But then he said no more.

10:23.000 --> 10:27.950
My mobile phone beeped.

10:28.000 --> 10:30.950
You have one new message, it said.

10:31.000 --> 10:33.950
I pressed, read.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.950
Have a sad holiday.

10:37.000 --> 10:38.950
I pressed eliminate.

10:39.000 --> 10:42.950
It was from one of the horrible girls at school.

10:43.000 --> 10:44.950
I switched my phone off.

10:45.000 --> 10:47.950
I needed to forget about them.

10:48.000 --> 10:50.950
The roads were very narrow now.

10:51.000 --> 10:52.950
We are nearly home.

10:53.000 --> 10:54.950
Said my uncle.

10:55.000 --> 10:56.950
I stared at him.

10:57.000 --> 10:58.950
We couldn't be nearly home.

10:59.000 --> 11:01.950
We were in the countryside.

11:02.000 --> 11:08.950
I could see some small houses, lots of animals and grass, but there was no town.

11:09.000 --> 11:12.950
Uncle Fraser turned right into a small track.

11:13.000 --> 11:14.950
Home, Darwin?

11:15.000 --> 11:17.950
Uncle Fraser said to the pony.

11:18.000 --> 11:22.950
Darwin walked slowly because there were chickens running in front of him.

11:23.000 --> 11:29.950
At the end of the track, there was a little white house with a front garden full of flowers.

11:30.000 --> 11:30.950
In one field,

11:31.000 --> 11:35.950
I could see four cows waiting patiently by the gate.

11:36.000 --> 11:39.950
And in another, there were some goats and a donkey.

11:40.000 --> 11:40.950
We are home.

11:41.000 --> 11:42.950
Said Uncle Fraser.

11:43.000 --> 11:46.000
Welcome to White Heather Cottage.

11:50.000 --> 11:52.000
